    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Corbin Carroll** (78.80) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), both of whom are set to exploit favorable matchups against Kyle Freeland and Merrill Kelly. **Mickey Moniak** is particularly well-positioned today, benefiting from a massive +14% park boost and the high likelihood of swiping bags against Kelly\u2019s slow delivery, a critical factor in our strategy to maximize stolen base efficiency. **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.72) and **Josh Naylor** (73.26) anchor the core, with both projected to capitalize on shaky starts from Tyler Mahle and Randy V\u00e1squez. **James Wood** (68.08) remains a high-floor play in the leadoff spot; his ability to translate a solid 0.380 xwOBA into scoring opportunities against Shane Baz makes him a cornerstone for run production today.\n\nThe tightest decision on the roster involves **Austin Riley** (44.09), who was relegated to the bench despite his pedigree. While **Austin Riley** offers power, his negative SP Skill adjustment (-19%) against a tough arm like Early tipped the scales in favor of the higher-efficiency volume offered by **Brice Turang** and **Zach McKinstry**. We are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, specifically for **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Josh Naylor**. **Dalton Rushing** is a notable risk today; while he offers a strong platoon advantage, his projected #7 spot in the lineup limits his ceiling, and we are keeping a close eye on confirmation to ensure he doesn't slip below our minimum efficiency floor. With **Jose Caballero** and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, but the projected outputs for **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.35) and **Gabriel Moreno** (60.50) ensure we remain competitive across all five categories.",
